  "result": "Excellent! The foreign currency support has been successfully implemented. Here's what was added:\n\n**src/money.js** \u2014 Added:\n\n1. **RATES export** \u2014 Exchange rates (units of that currency per euro):\n   - `EUR: 1` (1 euro = 1 EUR)\n   - `USD: 1.085` (1 euro = 1.085 USD)\n   - `GBP: 0.8425` (1 euro = 0.8425 GBP)\n\n2. **convert(cents, currency)** function:\n   - Converts euro cents to another currency's cents\n   - Returns `ok(converted_cents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n   - Uses `roundCents()` to ensure integer cent results\n   - Handles negative amounts correctly\n\n3. **formatMoney(cents, currency)** function:\n   - Formats amounts with appropriate currency symbol:\n     - `$` for USD (e.g., `$1,234.56`)\n     - `\u00a3` for GBP (e.g., `\u00a31,234.56`)\n     - `\u20ac` for EUR (e.g., `\u20ac1,234.56`)\n   - Includes thousands separators\n   - Shows 2 decimal places\n   - Handles negative amounts with sign prefix\n   - Uses `?` for unknown currencies\n\n**test/money.test.js** \u2014 Added 17 comprehensive tests covering:\n- RATES constant values\n- EUR to EUR conversion (identity)\n- EUR to USD conversion with correct rate\n- EUR to GBP conversion with correct rate\n- Unknown currency returns error\n- Zero amount conversion\n- Integer cent results\n- Negative amount handling\n- Format with EUR, USD, GBP symbols\n- Thousands separators in formatting\n- Large amount formatting\n- Unknown currency formatting\n- Zero amount formatting\n- Chained convert and format operations\n- Fractional conversion accuracy\n- Consistent sign placement\n\n**All 286 tests pass** \u2713",
